Subject: [PATCH] FFT: the fitter-routing census gate 37 at main+0x46f250
 (0084)

The E2 device round blanked the side-mask textures via DM_ROMFS_OVERLAY with the
mount provably overlaid and the bars measured pixel-identical, so the bars are
drawn geometry. The probe re-parse settled the mechanism: the battle layer
reaches the fitter with its own float rect (32, 0, 1632, 888) = 0.85*1920 and the
fitter centers that width (FIT_B (144, 0, 1776, 888) = the 144-px bars). The
rect writer is runtime arithmetic (all static sweeps exhausted), so gate 37
censuses the routing cbz (flag [x21+0x1ec], object x21 + vtable, stack rect,
input floats) that both fitter paths share, to guard a consumer-side cut to the
battle layer before cutting.

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: revJ evidence round: the E2 device test blanked the two candidate side-mask textures through DM_ROMFS_OVERLAY and the battle bars measured pixel-identical, so the bars are drawn geometry; the probe re-parse localizes them to the letterbox fitter client layer whose float rect (32, 0, 1632, 888) = 0.85*1920 is centered into the frame (FIT_B (144, 0, 1776, 888)). The rect writer is runtime arithmetic, so gate 37 (FIT_ROUTE) censuses the routing cbz both fitter paths share (flag, object, vtable, stack rect, input floats) to guard a consumer-side cut to the battle layer only, since small UI rects also pass the same callsite and must not become full-screen before the next device evidence round.
Issue: mexicanstratocaster/NX2Apple-edgy#1

